                <pb facs="0701" n="529" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg529"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 341.622a/316</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-05-31T14:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 31, 1917, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 2.50 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6318. Your telegram 4747, May [<hi rendition="#italic">April</hi>] 23, 4 p.m.,
                    last paragraph. British Government while equally reserving all such rights as
                    they may possess are most willing that there should be reciprocal action between
                    the two Governments and that United States warships should remove enemy subjects
                    or agents from British ships if any such ships carrying persons of this
                    description are encountered.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
